# A compacted database's header: generation 2.
# It's the header of file-compacted.hex. It continues from the last batch
# of file-new.hex: generation 1, sequence number 3.
# See beta/FORMAT.md. Every fixture uses the database ID 0123456789abcdef fedcba9876543210.

48 43 52 58 0d 0a 1a 0a                           # header: magic number, "HCRX" then CR, LF, Ctrl-Z, LF
01 00 00 00                                       # format version: 1
01 23 45 67 89 ab cd ef fe dc ba 98 76 54 32 10   # database ID
02 00 00 00 00 00 00 00                           # generation: 2
01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00                           # continues from: generation 1
03 00 00 00 00 00 00 00                           # continues from: sequence number 3
41 64 3f 11                                       # continues from: checksum 0x113f6441
cd 01 00 00 00 00 00 00                           # compacted part ends at offset 461
7c cc 45 f4                                       # header checksum: 0xf445cc7c, the CRC32C of bytes 0 to 63
